* ori.w/andi.w to ccr (an r68 source's ori.w #Carry,ccr): the byte form, as both Microware
* assemblers take it (Ultra C's with a warning), and so a byte immediate of an external relocated
* as the whole word (byte-imm-ext), one known only later written as the whole word
* (byte-imm-later); a0f6d83 and bfaa6ae took only .b or no size to ccr.
* fixed: 1d7ce3b 2026-10-15 r68togas: .w to ccr is the byte form for the byte immediates; quotes in error texts as backquotes
* expect text: 003c0000 023cfffe 4e71 4e71
* expect reloc: 00000002 R_68K_16          Ext_a
 psect ccr_word,0,0,0,0,0
 ori.w #Ext_a,ccr
 andi.w #Val_b,ccr
 nop
Val_b equ -2
 ends
